  <prompt>
    Make the three-pane workspace COORDINATE for real, and prove it with a real-PaneEventBus cross-pane
    test. Today the R2 differentiator is stub-only despite task 070 being open and Flows 1&2 being "wired":
    4 of 6 compose flows are stub/contract-only; the Flow 1&2 receivers are LOG-ONLY and sit on the WRONG
    pane (ComposeWorkspace, not the Context/Assistant panes that should react); only Flow 5 is genuinely
    wired; and none of the 6 `compose_*` discriminants exist in the typed bus union — they all ride via
    `as any`, an ADR-030 violation. Close register Cluster 5 gaps 5.1–5.2: put REAL receivers on the
    Context and Assistant panes, build Flows 3/4/6, and add the typed discriminants so no compose event
    rides untyped. Land a real-bus cross-pane integration test as the anti-recurrence forcing function
    (evidence the receivers are mounted + reachable, per the project E2E definition-of-done row 3).
    This task supersedes and absorbs task 070.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend developer fluent in the SpaarkeAi three-pane shell (ThreePaneShell, ContextPaneController,
    ConversationPane), the PaneEventBus contract (@spaarke/events-components) and its compose-contracts.ts
    discriminants, and the ComposeWorkspace/ComposeEditor emit sites. Comfortable writing a real-bus jest
    integration test that drives a compose event across panes.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Emitting each of the six compose flow signals on the PaneEventBus produces the correct cross-pane
    effect: the Context pane and the Assistant/Conversation pane react on their OWN controllers (not a
    log-only handler on ComposeWorkspace). Flows 3, 4, and 6 are built (not stubs). All six `compose_*`
    signals are typed discriminants in the bus union — zero `as any`. A real-PaneEventBus jest test drives
    each flow emit → asserts the receiving pane's observable effect. Cluster 5 gaps 5.1–5.2 closed; task
    070 folded in and marked superseded.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source of truth: notes/e2e-gap-register.md Cluster 5 (gaps 5.1–5.2) with file:line evidence, and
      design.md §7 (three-pane flow catalog) + §7.2 (the RETRACTED "invented" discriminants — do NOT
      reintroduce compose_action_request / compose_edit_apply_request; the real discriminants are in
      compose-contracts.ts). Spike 0 forbids inventing new discriminant names; extend the EXISTING typed
      union. The real apply/selection flows already in code (compose_selection_offer,
      compose_assistant_insert with ledgerRef) are the pattern — mirror them for the typed union; do NOT
      change their runtime contract.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="flow-receivers-context" edit="true">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/shell/ContextPaneController.tsx (~433-489, the default:break) — add REAL receivers for the Context-pane flows (Flow 6 doc-context surfacing + the context legs of 3/4) instead of falling through default.</file>
      <file purpose="flow-receivers-assistant" edit="true">SpaarkeAi ConversationPane / Assistant-pane controller — add REAL receivers for the Assistant-pane flows (the conversation legs of Flows 3/4) so the Assistant reacts on its own controller.</file>
      <file purpose="wrong-pane-stub" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (~706-732) — the log-only Flow 1&2 receivers on the WRONG pane: move the reaction to the correct pane controller (Context/Assistant); ComposeWorkspace should EMIT/relay, not be the terminal handler for cross-pane flows.</file>
      <file purpose="typed-discriminants" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (~554-565) — remove the `as any` emits; use the typed discriminants.</file>
      <file purpose="bus-union" edit="true">the compose-contracts.ts / PaneEventBus typed union (@spaarke/events-components or the compose widget contracts file) — add the 6 compose_* discriminants to the typed union so every compose event is typed. Do NOT add the retracted invented names.</file>
      <file purpose="e2e-test" edit="true">a NEW real-PaneEventBus jest integration test (co-located with the three-pane shell tests) — the anti-recurrence forcing function: emit each flow → assert the receiving pane's effect.</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">Every compose event on the bus MUST use a typed discriminant in the union — zero `as any`. This is the core contract fix (gap 5.2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-invented-discriminants">Do NOT reintroduce the retracted invented names compose_action_request / compose_edit_apply_request (design §7.2 / Spike 0 forbid them). Extend the EXISTING discriminants in compose-contracts.ts. Do NOT change the runtime contract of the already-shipped compose_selection_offer / compose_assistant_insert flows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="correct-pane">Receivers live on the pane that OWNS the reaction (ContextPaneController for context surfacing, the Assistant/Conversation controller for conversation reactions) — NOT a log-only handler on ComposeWorkspace. ComposeWorkspace emits/relays; it is not the terminal cross-pane handler.</constraint>
    <constraint source="reuse-070">This task supersedes 070 — fold 070's intent in; do NOT leave a parallel 070 implementation. One coherent coordination layer, not two (Component Justification §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="real-bus-test">The forcing function MUST use the REAL PaneEventBus (not a mocked bus) and assert a cross-pane effect (emit on pane A → observable reaction on pane B). An isolated unit test that only checks a handler in isolation does NOT satisfy the project E2E definition-of-done row 3 (mounted + reachable).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-defer">Build Flows 3/4/6 in this pass; do NOT stub them or file deferrals for in-scope flows. 072 (Doc Q&A) inherits this Context surfacing (Flow 6) — leave it consumable, but building 072 itself is out of scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-http">This is a client-only coordination task — no BFF/endpoint changes. If a flow genuinely needs a server round-trip, that is an escalation, not a silent BFF edit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>three-pane-coordination, pane-event-bus, compose-contracts-discriminants, real-bus-jest</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/e2e-gap-register.md</file>
