      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the register Cluster 5 + this POML + compose-contracts.ts. Read the 6 flows in design §7, the retracted names in §7.2 (do NOT use them), and the current emit/receive sites (ComposeWorkspace ~706-732, ContextPaneController ~433-489 default:break, ComposeEditor ~554-565 `as any`). Enumerate which of the 6 flows are already wired (Flow 5) vs stub (3/4/6) vs log-only-wrong-pane (1/2).</step>
    <step order="1">Typed discriminants (gap 5.2): add the 6 compose_* discriminants to the typed bus union in compose-contracts.ts, mirroring the shape of the existing compose_selection_offer / compose_assistant_insert; remove every `as any` emit in ComposeEditor and elsewhere.</step>
    <step order="2">Correct-pane receivers (gap 5.1, Flows 1&2): move the log-only ComposeWorkspace receivers to the Context/Assistant pane controllers so the owning pane reacts; ComposeWorkspace emits/relays only.</step>
    <step order="3">Build Flows 3, 4, 6 (gap 5.1): implement the real receivers + effects on the correct pane controllers (Flow 6 = doc-context surfacing on Context pane; Flows 3/4 = their context + conversation legs). Fold in task 070's intent — one coordination layer.</step>
    <step order="4">ANTI-RECURRENCE TEST (definition-of-done, non-waivable): add a real-PaneEventBus jest integration test that, for each of the 6 flows, emits on the source pane and asserts the receiving pane's observable effect — evidence the receivers are mounted + reachable (project E2E DoD row 3). No mocked bus.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify: Compose.Components + SpaarkeAi + events-components tsc clean (your files); jest (new real-bus test + regression). Run Step 9.5 (code-review + adr-check) UNCONDITIONALLY — confirm zero `as any` on compose events and no invented discriminants. Update this POML notes; mark 070 superseded in your report. Do NOT edit TASK-INDEX/current-task (main session reconciles). No BFF publish-size needed (client-only) — state that explicitly.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">compose-contracts.ts (6 compose_* discriminants added to the typed union)</output>
    <output type="code">ContextPaneController.tsx + ConversationPane/Assistant controller (real receivers for Flows 3/4/6 + relocated Flows 1/2)</output>
    <output type="code">ComposeWorkspace.tsx (emit/relay, not terminal handler) + ComposeEditor.tsx (typed emits, no `as any`)</output>
    <output type="test">real-PaneEventBus cross-pane jest integration test (6 flows: emit → receiving-pane effect)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">All six compose flow signals produce the correct cross-pane effect on the OWNING pane controller (Context / Assistant), not a log-only handler on ComposeWorkspace (gap 5.1 closed; Flows 1&2 relocated, 3/4/6 built).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All six compose_* signals are typed discriminants in the bus union; zero `as any` on compose events; the retracted invented names are NOT reintroduced (gap 5.2 / ADR-030 closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A real-PaneEventBus jest integration test drives each of the 6 flow emits and asserts the receiving pane's observable effect (anti-recurrence definition-of-done row 3; real bus, not mocked).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 070 is folded in / superseded — one coordination layer, no parallel 070 implementation left behind.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The already-shipped compose_selection_offer / compose_assistant_insert runtime contracts are unchanged; Flow 5 still works.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">tsc + jest green for the touched packages; Step 9.5 clean; no BFF changes (client-only, stated explicitly).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

